("place.contact", "isa", "Place")
("place.contact", "slug", "contact")
("place.contact", "route", "places/contact.html")
("place.contact", "title", "Beautiful words. The wrong answer.")
("place.contact", "lead", "An answer can sound convincing while missing what someone meant.")
("place.contact", "region", "Contact & correction")
("place.contact", "chapter", "06")
("place.contact", "source", "note.contact")
("place.contact", "light", "human")
("place.contact", "paragraph", "In the recorded exchange, an explanation brought ideas from an earlier discussion into a different question. The words fitted together, but the explanation had lost touch with the person speaking.")
("place.contact", "paragraph", "The interpretation was withdrawn. The next inquiry began with the particular mistake: what had been misunderstood, and what would a more relevant answer do differently?")
("place.contact", "fullParagraph", "One inquiry began when a polished explanation imported an old framework into a different question. It sounded coherent. It had missed the person speaking.")
("place.contact", "fullParagraph", "The interpretation was withdrawn. The next inquiry began with the recognition of that failure, then used contrast cases and competing explanations to investigate it.")
("place.contact", "choice", "place.contact.choice.0")
("place.contact.choice.0", "destination", "place.listening")
("place.contact.choice.0", "label", "What was the person trying to do?")
("place.contact.choice.0", "kind", "Look more closely")
("place.contact", "choice", "place.contact.choice.1")
("place.contact.choice.1", "destination", "place.sourcery")
("place.contact.choice.1", "label", "What should a machine help us do?")
("place.contact.choice.1", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.contact", "choice", "place.contact.choice.2")
("place.contact.choice.2", "destination", "place.care")
("place.contact.choice.2", "label", "Come back to care")
("place.contact.choice.2", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.contact", "choice", "place.contact.choice.3")
("place.contact.choice.3", "destination", "place.observation")
("place.contact.choice.3", "label", "What else does a representation leave out?")
("place.contact.choice.3", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.kenosis", "isa", "Place")
("place.kenosis", "slug", "kenosis")
("place.kenosis", "route", "places/kenosis.html")
("place.kenosis", "title", "If you could control everything, should you?")
("place.kenosis", "lead", "Being able to control something does not settle whether you should.")
("place.kenosis", "region", "Power & agency")
("place.kenosis", "chapter", "07")
("place.kenosis", "source", "note.kenosis")
("place.kenosis", "light", "boundary")
("place.kenosis", "paragraph", "Kenosis is a Christian word often translated as “self-emptying.” Here it means choosing to use power in ways that give others room to act, rather than taking over their choices.")
("place.kenosis", "paragraph", "Making room does not mean leaving people unprotected. If one person is taking away another’s freedom, care may require a boundary or an intervention. Ask whose freedom your restraint protects, and whose needs it may overlook.")
("place.kenosis", "paragraph", "This is a philosophical and theological argument. It is not a scientific rule or an instruction about your own relationships.")
("place.kenosis", "fullParagraph", "Kenosis asks how power can make room for another person’s agency. Restraint, trust and formation matter. So do protection and responsibility.")
("place.kenosis", "fullParagraph", "The difficult boundary is where restraint permits one person to destroy another’s effective agency. Care can require intervention.")
("place.kenosis", "word", "word.kenosis")
("place.kenosis", "word", "word.agency")
("place.kenosis", "choice", "place.kenosis.choice.0")
("place.kenosis.choice.0", "destination", "place.restraint")
("place.kenosis.choice.0", "label", "When does leaving room leave someone exposed?")
("place.kenosis.choice.0", "kind", "Look more closely")
("place.kenosis", "choice", "place.kenosis.choice.1")
("place.kenosis.choice.1", "destination", "place.care")
("place.kenosis.choice.1", "label", "Who is carrying the cost?")
("place.kenosis.choice.1", "kind", "Follow the human question")
("place.kenosis", "choice", "place.kenosis.choice.2")
("place.kenosis.choice.2", "destination", "place.sourcery")
("place.kenosis.choice.2", "label", "Build systems people can understand and direct")
("place.kenosis.choice.2", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.kenosis", "choice", "place.kenosis.choice.3")
("place.kenosis.choice.3", "destination", "place.personal")
("place.kenosis.choice.3", "label", "Why I took this question seriously")
("place.kenosis.choice.3", "kind", "Personal account")
("place.kenosis", "choice", "place.kenosis.choice.4")
("place.kenosis.choice.4", "destination", "place.coexistence")
("place.kenosis.choice.4", "label", "Who lives with the consequences?")
("place.kenosis.choice.4", "kind", "A path into the wider world")
("place.sourcery", "isa", "Place")
("place.sourcery", "slug", "sourcery")
("place.sourcery", "route", "places/sourcery.html")
("place.sourcery", "title", "More help from machines. More say for people.")
("place.sourcery", "lead", "Let machines help with the work while people keep a meaningful say in what is made.")
("place.sourcery", "region", "Sourcery")
("place.sourcery", "chapter", "08")
("place.sourcery", "source", "note.authorship")
("place.sourcery", "light", "boundary")
("place.sourcery", "paragraph", "AI can help write software, suggest changes and run checks. People still decide what is worth making, who it serves and whether it is good.")
("place.sourcery", "paragraph", "The aim is to make a system’s workings understandable and changeable. You should be able to follow an idea back to its source and ask what was checked. The workshop lets you try this with two small edits.")
("place.sourcery", "fullParagraph", "The aim is to let AI take on more programming work while people retain expertise, taste, discretion and responsibility. People decide what is worth making, who it serves and whether the experience is good.")
("place.sourcery", "fullParagraph", "Open architecture should mean more than being handed source code. It should let you understand the decisions, follow a value to its source, challenge a rule and change the workings. The architecture should remain revisable.")
("place.sourcery", "fullParagraph", "Assurance should fit the consequences. A typed check, an automated test, a human review and independent verification are different kinds of evidence. We should say which happened, against which version, and what remains unknown.")
("place.sourcery", "fullParagraph", "AI can remain a collaborator throughout. The intention is to make expertise go further; any claim about productivity or jobs would need evidence of its own.")
("place.sourcery", "word", "word.authorship")
("place.sourcery", "choice", "place.sourcery.choice.0")
("place.sourcery.choice.0", "destination", "place.workshop")
("place.sourcery.choice.0", "label", "Try a change and follow its consequences")
("place.sourcery.choice.0", "kind", "Enter the workshop")
("place.sourcery", "choice", "place.sourcery.choice.1")
("place.sourcery.choice.1", "destination", "place.representation")
("place.sourcery.choice.1", "label", "What should a map tell us about its limits?")
("place.sourcery.choice.1", "kind", "Look more closely")
("place.sourcery", "choice", "place.sourcery.choice.2")
("place.sourcery.choice.2", "destination", "place.contact")
("place.sourcery.choice.2", "label", "What does the model fail to hear?")
("place.sourcery.choice.2", "kind", "Another way back")
("place.sourcery", "choice", "place.sourcery.choice.3")
("place.sourcery.choice.3", "destination", "place.kenosis")
("place.sourcery.choice.3", "label", "What should power leave alone?")
("place.sourcery.choice.3", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.sourcery", "choice", "place.sourcery.choice.4")
("place.sourcery.choice.4", "destination", "place.care")
("place.sourcery.choice.4", "label", "Keep care in the loop")
("place.sourcery.choice.4", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.monster", "isa", "Place")
("place.monster", "slug", "monster")
("place.monster", "route", "places/monster.html")
("place.monster", "title", "A matching number is only a clue.")
("place.monster", "lead", "A matching number is a clue. It does not identify the thing you found.")
("place.monster", "region", "The Monster trail")
("place.monster", "chapter", "09")
("place.monster", "source", "note.monster")
("place.monster", "light", "unseen")
("place.monster", "paragraph", "The research compares three mathematical structures. One broad measurement makes them look alike. A more detailed count gives three different answers: 744, 24 and 0.")
("place.monster", "paragraph", "Switch the view to see the counts. They separate these three chosen structures. They do not prove that a physical object contains the structure nicknamed the Monster.")
("place.monster", "fullParagraph", "Three rank-24 candidates share the same coarse thermal signature. Their weight-one current dimensions—744, 24 and 0—separate the declared E₈³, Leech and Moonshine family.")
("place.monster", "fullParagraph", "Even that is one gate on a longer path. The physical carrier, boundary algebra and exclusive detector prediction still have to be established.")
("place.monster", "word", "word.model")
("place.monster", "instruction", "Compare the broad view with the detailed count. Which view tells the three structures apart?")
("place.monster", "choice", "place.monster.choice.0")
("place.monster.choice.0", "destination", "place.replay")
("place.monster.choice.0", "label", "What record could tell the structures apart?")
("place.monster.choice.0", "kind", "Look more closely")
("place.monster", "choice", "place.monster.choice.1")
("place.monster.choice.1", "destination", "place.observation")
("place.monster.choice.1", "label", "Return to what the detector discards")
("place.monster.choice.1", "kind", "Another way back")
("place.monster", "choice", "place.monster.choice.2")
("place.monster.choice.2", "destination", "place.instrument")
("place.monster.choice.2", "label", "Explore the smaller experiment")
("place.monster.choice.2", "kind", "Follow the research")
("place.monster", "choice", "place.monster.choice.3")
("place.monster.choice.3", "destination", "place.sourcery")
("place.monster.choice.3", "label", "How could many people explore this together?")
("place.monster.choice.3", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.calibration", "isa", "Place")
("place.calibration", "slug", "calibration")
("place.calibration", "route", "places/calibration.html")
("place.calibration", "title", "Before you trust the reading, check the ruler.")
("place.calibration", "lead", "Before trusting a number, check what the tool can measure.")
("place.calibration", "region", "The borrowed ruler")
("place.calibration", "chapter", "10")
("place.calibration", "source", "note.detector")
("place.calibration", "light", "unseen")
("place.calibration", "paragraph", "Three rulers can agree and still all be stretched. More readings help only when you know how the tools relate to what you are measuring.")
("place.calibration", "paragraph", "Move the measuring axis in the drawing. The same difference can be hidden from one direction and visible from another. This is a small example, separate from the larger research model.")
("place.calibration", "fullParagraph", "The hidden-plane example does not say that any collection of extra channels will reveal the answer. The ports must reach the relevant subspace, and their relationship to the system must be calibrated. More readings are useful only if you know what they are readings of.")
("place.calibration", "fullParagraph", "Imagine measuring a table with three rulers that all stretched in the same heat. Agreement would be reassuring. It would not supply the missing reference. This is an analogy for the question of access and calibration, not a further result of the finite model.")
("place.calibration", "fullParagraph", "Before asking what the system did, ask what the apparatus could distinguish. Which states would still look identical through these ports? A blank region on that map is a reason to design another measurement.")
("place.calibration", "word", "word.calibration")
("place.calibration", "pause", "What would remain invisible even if every reading agreed?")
("place.calibration", "instruction", "Move the slider. Watch how turning the measuring line changes the number.")
("place.calibration", "choice", "place.calibration.choice.0")
("place.calibration.choice.0", "destination", "place.instrument")
("place.calibration.choice.0", "label", "Return to the measuring tool")
("place.calibration.choice.0", "kind", "Follow the research")
("place.calibration", "choice", "place.calibration.choice.1")
("place.calibration.choice.1", "destination", "place.replay")
("place.calibration.choice.1", "label", "Let someone check the record")
("place.calibration.choice.1", "kind", "Follow the research")
("place.calibration", "choice", "place.calibration.choice.2")
("place.calibration.choice.2", "destination", "place.listening")
("place.calibration.choice.2", "label", "And when the instrument is a question?")
("place.calibration.choice.2", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.replay", "isa", "Place")
("place.replay", "slug", "replay")
("place.replay", "route", "places/replay.html")
("place.replay", "title", "Can someone else check the result?")
("place.replay", "lead", "Keep enough of the method for someone else to check the result.")
("place.replay", "region", "The replay room")
("place.replay", "chapter", "11")
("place.replay", "source", "note.instrument")
("place.replay", "light", "unseen")
("place.replay", "paragraph", "A final number is hard to check on its own. The computer experiment also keeps its starting settings, several measurements and the results of comparison runs.")
("place.replay", "paragraph", "A separate checking program repeats the calculations from those saved settings. That checks the computer result. It does not replace a test with real equipment.")
("place.replay", "fullParagraph", "The four-mode virtual instrument retains more than a returned angle. Its record includes a complex return matrix, populations, loss, control work and the configuration that produced them. A separate verifier replays the saved configuration and checks those records.")
("place.replay", "fullParagraph", "The documented design crosses two model settings with four rates and three path controls: forward, reverse and fixed. Those comparisons make a more demanding question possible. Does the proposed effect survive the controls, and what changes when declared imperfections are included?")
("place.replay", "fullParagraph", "This room describes that recorded software experiment. It does not run it in your browser, and a successful numerical replay does not supply a physical apparatus. The next threshold remains an actual acquisition with its own calibration and uncertainties.")
("place.replay", "word", "word.replay")
("place.replay", "word", "word.control")
("place.replay", "pause", "What would another person need to discover that your result was wrong?")
("place.replay", "choice", "place.replay.choice.0")
("place.replay.choice.0", "destination", "place.monster")
("place.replay.choice.0", "label", "Ask a rival to disagree")
("place.replay.choice.0", "kind", "Follow the research")
("place.replay", "choice", "place.replay.choice.1")
("place.replay.choice.1", "destination", "place.representation")
("place.replay.choice.1", "label", "Keep the conditions attached")
("place.replay.choice.1", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.replay", "choice", "place.replay.choice.2")
("place.replay.choice.2", "destination", "place.calibration")
("place.replay.choice.2", "label", "Check what the measuring tools can see")
("place.replay.choice.2", "kind", "Another way back")
("place.water", "isa", "Place")
("place.water", "slug", "water")
("place.water", "route", "places/water.html")
("place.water", "title", "The horse has a few questions.")
("place.water", "lead", "The guide offers a lesson. The horse has noticed something else.")
("place.water", "region", "The water’s edge")
("place.water", "chapter", "12")
("place.water", "source", "note.reflection")
("place.water", "light", "human")
("place.water", "paragraph", "The guide points at the water. The horse looks down. There is already a horse in there, and it seems to have strong opinions about the guide. Nobody mentioned a committee.")
("place.water", "paragraph", "Perhaps the next explanation can wait. What is the horse being invited into? The guide can look at the reflection too. You can read the little fable your own way—or just enjoy a horse declining a well-prepared presentation.")
("place.water", "fullParagraph", "The guide points at the water. The horse looks down. There is already a horse in there, and it appears to have strong opinions about the guide. Nobody mentioned a committee.")
("place.water", "fullParagraph", "Perhaps the next explanation can wait. In this little fable, the offered lesson has become an encounter with the person trying to offer it. The guide can inspect the water too. What looked like refusal might reveal something about the invitation.")
("place.water", "fullParagraph", "You are free to read the reflection differently—or simply enjoy a horse declining a very well-prepared presentation. The story has no access to your private reasons. It can offer a surface to look into, then leave you room to decide what you see.")
("place.water", "pause", "When you offer someone an answer, what else might they be encountering?")
("place.water", "choice", "place.water.choice.0")
("place.water.choice.0", "destination", "place.listening")
("place.water.choice.0", "label", "Put down the presentation")
("place.water.choice.0", "kind", "Reflective passage")
("place.water", "choice", "place.water.choice.1")
("place.water.choice.1", "destination", "place.discomfort")
("place.water.choice.1", "label", "Look at the inconvenient reflection")
("place.water.choice.1", "kind", "Reflective passage")
("place.water", "choice", "place.water.choice.2")
("place.water.choice.2", "destination", "place.care")
("place.water.choice.2", "label", "Sit by the water a while")
("place.water.choice.2", "kind", "Another way back")
("place.discomfort", "isa", "Place")
("place.discomfort", "slug", "discomfort")
("place.discomfort", "route", "places/discomfort.html")
("place.discomfort", "title", "Truth hurts. So can being wrong.")
("place.discomfort", "lead", "Feeling hurt does not tell us, by itself, which explanation is true.")
("place.discomfort", "region", "The inconvenient truth")
("place.discomfort", "chapter", "13")
("place.discomfort", "source", "note.reflection")
("place.discomfort", "light", "human")
("place.discomfort", "paragraph", "A fact can challenge an explanation we care about. So can a mistaken accusation. The discomfort alone cannot tell us which one we are facing.")
("place.discomfort", "paragraph", "Try separating what happened, what you think it means, and how it feels. Which part could you check with a source or a fresh question? You do not need to share a personal experience with this story.")
("place.discomfort", "fullParagraph", "Suppose a fact threatens an explanation you have worked hard to build. You can defend the explanation, discard it, or slow down enough to distinguish the record from what you have made it mean. None of those movements becomes correct simply because it feels difficult.")
("place.discomfort", "fullParagraph", "“Truth hurts” is Aaron’s originating phrase for this reflective territory. Here it becomes a question rather than a verdict. Discomfort might accompany an unwelcome fact, a mistaken accusation, an incomplete account, or the discovery that your own frame has become too small.")
("place.discomfort", "fullParagraph", "The invitation is to find a check outside the feeling: a source, a contrast case, a question you can ask again. You need not confess anything to the story. Carry the question privately, or leave it here.")
("place.discomfort", "pause", "Which part can you check without first deciding who was right?")
("place.discomfort", "choice", "place.discomfort.choice.0")
("place.discomfort.choice.0", "destination", "place.contact")
("place.discomfort.choice.0", "label", "See an explanation actually withdrawn")
("place.discomfort.choice.0", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.discomfort", "choice", "place.discomfort.choice.1")
("place.discomfort.choice.1", "destination", "place.revision")
("place.discomfort.choice.1", "label", "Keep a way to change your mind")
("place.discomfort.choice.1", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.discomfort", "choice", "place.discomfort.choice.2")
("place.discomfort.choice.2", "destination", "place.water")
("place.discomfort.choice.2", "label", "Visit the uncooperative horse")
("place.discomfort.choice.2", "kind", "Reflective passage")
("place.listening", "isa", "Place")
("place.listening", "slug", "listening")
("place.listening", "route", "places/listening.html")
("place.listening", "title", "What are they trying to do?")
("place.listening", "lead", "Before answering, ask what the other person is trying to do.")
("place.listening", "region", "The unasked question")
("place.listening", "chapter", "14")
("place.listening", "source", "note.contact")
("place.listening", "light", "human")
("place.listening", "paragraph", "Someone might be asking for a solution, testing an idea, telling you something difficult, or asking to be heard. A polished answer to a different request can still miss the point.")
("place.listening", "paragraph", "Try the conversation. You can choose another reply and see another possible response. It is a fictional example, not a test of your listening skills or a way to read someone’s mind.")
("place.listening", "fullParagraph", "In the recorded correction, the failure was more specific than an incorrect sentence. An earlier framework had captured a new inquiry. Shared conversation history was mistaken for continuity of subject. The response had stopped following the person who was speaking.")
("place.listening", "fullParagraph", "The successor inquiry proposes several alignments to examine: the subject, the speaker’s intention, the scale of the answer, the relevance of old context and the consequence of replying this way. These are candidate cues from a case, not a universal instrument for reading people.")
("place.listening", "fullParagraph", "Try the question on an ordinary encounter: is the person requesting a solution, testing an idea, telling you something, or asking to be heard? The answer remains theirs to correct. A useful first move can be an interpretation light enough to put down.")
("place.listening", "pause", "What would you ask if your favourite explanation were unavailable?")
("place.listening", "instruction", "Choose a reply, then read the possible response. You can try every reply.")
("place.listening", "choice", "place.listening.choice.0")
("place.listening.choice.0", "destination", "place.contact")
("place.listening.choice.0", "label", "Read the original mismatch")
("place.listening.choice.0", "kind", "Read a related account")
("place.listening", "choice", "place.listening.choice.1")
("place.listening.choice.1", "destination", "place.water")
("place.listening.choice.1", "label", "Hear from the horse")
("place.listening.choice.1", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.listening", "choice", "place.listening.choice.2")
("place.listening.choice.2", "destination", "place.restraint")
("place.listening.choice.2", "label", "Leave room for an answer")
("place.listening.choice.2", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.restraint", "isa", "Place")
("place.restraint", "slug", "restraint")
("place.restraint", "route", "places/restraint.html")
("place.restraint", "title", "Leaving room is still a choice.")
("place.restraint", "lead", "Holding back can give someone room. It can also leave someone exposed.")
("place.restraint", "region", "The open hand")
("place.restraint", "chapter", "15")
("place.restraint", "source", "note.kenosis")
("place.restraint", "light", "boundary")
("place.restraint", "paragraph", "The argument asks how power can help other people make real choices. Taking over every decision can remove the freedom we say we want to support.")
("place.restraint", "paragraph", "But holding back is not always helpful. If someone is taking away another person’s freedom, protection may be needed. Ask who gains room to act, and who is left carrying the cost.")
("place.restraint", "fullParagraph", "The kenotic argument treats power as something governed by love rather than exhausted by control. Making room for another agent is a positive commitment: their choices must be consequential enough to count as their own.")
("place.restraint", "fullParagraph", "That commitment is not an absolute rule against intervention. The same argument retains boundaries and responsibility for protection. If one agent is consuming another’s effective freedom, leaving the arrangement alone can preserve domination rather than make room for agency.")
("place.restraint", "fullParagraph", "This is a philosophical boundary to examine, not an instruction about your own situation. Ask whose room is growing, whose is shrinking, and what evidence would challenge the comfortable description of your choice.")
("place.restraint", "word", "word.agency")
("place.restraint", "word", "word.kenosis")
("place.restraint", "pause", "Whose freedom does this restraint make possible?")
("place.restraint", "choice", "place.restraint.choice.0")
("place.restraint.choice.0", "destination", "place.permission")
("place.restraint.choice.0", "label", "Distinguish three different questions")
("place.restraint.choice.0", "kind", "Conceptual connection")
("place.restraint", "choice", "place.restraint.choice.1")
("place.restraint.choice.1", "destination", "place.care")
("place.restraint.choice.1", "label", "Ask who carries the cost")
("place.restraint.choice.1", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.restraint", "choice", "place.restraint.choice.2")
("place.restraint.choice.2", "destination", "place.kenosis")
("place.restraint.choice.2", "label", "Read the larger argument")
("place.restraint.choice.2", "kind", "Another way back")
("place.permission", "isa", "Place")
("place.permission", "slug", "permission")
("place.permission", "route", "places/permission.html")
("place.permission", "title", "I can. May I? Should I?")
("place.permission", "lead", "“Can I?”, “May I?” and “Should I?” are three different questions.")
("place.permission", "region", "Three doors")
("place.permission", "chapter", "16")
("place.permission", "source", "note.kenosis")
("place.permission", "light", "boundary")
("place.permission", "paragraph", "Being able to do something is about capability. Having permission is about who can authorize it. Deciding whether to do it also means considering the situation and its consequences.")
("place.permission", "paragraph", "Open the three doors. The example is a message that could change someone’s plans. No message is sent; the doors help you examine the decision.")
("place.permission", "fullParagraph", "Capability asks what an agent can bring about. Permission asks which actions are legitimate. Responsibility asks what the situation calls for among those possibilities. The kenotic synthesis separates these questions before developing its account of divine action.")
("place.permission", "fullParagraph", "The distinction also supplies an editorial question for machine delegation. A system may be able to generate a proposal, alter a record or carry out a plan. That ability alone cannot settle who should authorize the act or remain answerable for its consequences.")
("place.permission", "fullParagraph", "Notice where an interface makes these doors appear to be one door. A smooth path from suggestion to execution can conceal the moment at which another person’s judgment was needed. The design question is where to make that moment legible.")
("place.permission", "pause", "Which door have you been treating as if it opened the other two?")
("place.permission", "instruction", "Open each door. Each asks a different question about the same proposed action.")
("place.permission", "choice", "place.permission.choice.0")
("place.permission.choice.0", "destination", "place.sourcery")
("place.permission.choice.0", "label", "Take the question into a machine")
("place.permission.choice.0", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.permission", "choice", "place.permission.choice.1")
("place.permission.choice.1", "destination", "place.representation")
("place.permission.choice.1", "label", "Inspect what the proposal carries")
("place.permission.choice.1", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.permission", "choice", "place.permission.choice.2")
("place.permission.choice.2", "destination", "place.restraint")
("place.permission.choice.2", "label", "Return to the open hand")
("place.permission.choice.2", "kind", "Another way back")
("place.representation", "isa", "Place")
("place.representation", "slug", "representation")
("place.representation", "route", "places/representation.html")
("place.representation", "title", "Every map leaves something out.")
("place.representation", "lead", "A useful map leaves things out. We should be able to find out what.")
("place.representation", "region", "The mapmaker’s debt")
("place.representation", "chapter", "17")
("place.representation", "source", "note.sourcery")
("place.representation", "light", "boundary")
("place.representation", "paragraph", "A map makes some parts of the world easier to see. It also leaves out detail. A model, diagram or summary does the same.")
("place.representation", "paragraph", "Lift the layers of the map. Look for where the information came from, which assumptions it needs and what it cannot establish. A complete plan for an experiment does not prove that the experiment happened.")
("place.representation", "fullParagraph", "Programme algebra is a parallel representation of the corpus. Its declared purpose is to preserve structure, provenance and refused transformations in a compositional grammar. The prose sources retain their authority; a generated projection does not become an independently editable truth.")
("place.representation", "fullParagraph", "The source distinguishes several depths. Recording a document and its links is different from admitting a scientific transformation. A protocol can contain all required fields without the experiment ever having run. These differences need to survive the trip into a more convenient view.")
("place.representation", "fullParagraph", "Apply the same question to this expedition. A station is an authored reading, a passage is a proposed connection, and a field note describes its source and limit. Following a path does not prove the connection. This map owes you a way to see that distinction.")
("place.representation", "word", "word.representation")
("place.representation", "word", "word.assumption")
("place.representation", "pause", "What would become easier to misunderstand if this map looked authoritative?")
("place.representation", "instruction", "Open each layer to see what the map needs you to know.")
("place.representation", "choice", "place.representation.choice.0")
("place.representation.choice.0", "destination", "place.revision")
("place.representation.choice.0", "label", "Leave the correction visible")
("place.representation.choice.0", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.representation", "choice", "place.representation.choice.1")
("place.representation.choice.1", "destination", "place.replay")
("place.representation.choice.1", "label", "Ask for the actual record")
("place.representation.choice.1", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.representation", "choice", "place.representation.choice.2")
("place.representation.choice.2", "destination", "place.sourcery")
("place.representation.choice.2", "label", "Return to systems people can direct")
("place.representation.choice.2", "kind", "Another way back")
("place.representation", "choice", "place.representation.choice.3")
("place.representation.choice.3", "destination", "place.stone")
("place.representation.choice.3", "label", "Let an ordinary object open the map")
("place.representation.choice.3", "kind", "A path into the wider world")
("place.revision", "isa", "Place")
("place.revision", "slug", "revision")
("place.revision", "route", "places/revision.html")
("place.revision", "title", "Let the correction leave a seam.")
("place.revision", "lead", "When an explanation changes, leave a way to understand why.")
("place.revision", "region", "The visible seam")
("place.revision", "chapter", "18")
("place.revision", "source", "note.correction")
("place.revision", "light", "boundary")
("place.revision", "paragraph", "The collection keeps an earlier interpretation alongside the correction that withdrew it. That lets a reader see what went wrong and where the next inquiry began.")
("place.revision", "paragraph", "Open the correction. Keeping the change visible does not guarantee that every later claim is right. It gives someone else a better chance to question and check it.")
("place.revision", "fullParagraph", "The corpus retains the withdrawn cross-context interpretation as well as the inquiry that followed it. The predecessor imported physics into a different problem. Its withdrawal limits what readers should take from it; the successor begins again from the specific mismatch.")
("place.revision", "fullParagraph", "An immaculate story could smooth away that interruption. Keeping it visible makes another reading possible: the work did not become trustworthy by never losing contact. Here, a correction changed its direction. That is a particular retained event, not a guarantee about every later claim.")
("place.revision", "fullParagraph", "On returning to an earlier station, ask what you now read differently. The earlier scene has not secretly changed, and the site does not infer what you learned. The new perspective belongs to you. A route can finish with a more precise question.")
("place.revision", "pause", "What would you retain so a future reader could understand why you changed course?")
("place.revision", "instruction", "Open the correction to see why the earlier explanation was withdrawn.")
("place.revision", "choice", "place.revision.choice.0")
("place.revision.choice.0", "destination", "place.observation")
("place.revision.choice.0", "label", "Look at the first question again")
("place.revision.choice.0", "kind", "Another way back")
("place.revision", "choice", "place.revision.choice.1")
("place.revision.choice.1", "destination", "place.contact")
("place.revision.choice.1", "label", "Read the successor inquiry")
("place.revision.choice.1", "kind", "Read a related account")
("place.revision", "choice", "place.revision.choice.2")
("place.revision.choice.2", "destination", "place.discomfort")
("place.revision.choice.2", "label", "Stay with the discomfort")
("place.revision.choice.2", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.workshop", "isa", "Place")
("place.workshop", "slug", "workshop")
("place.workshop", "route", "places/workshop.html")
("place.workshop", "title", "Can you follow a change?")
("place.workshop", "lead", "Change a title or label, then see exactly what follows.")
("place.workshop", "region", "The workshop")
("place.workshop", "chapter", "19")
("place.workshop", "source", "note.authorship")
("place.workshop", "light", "boundary")
("place.workshop", "paragraph", "One story appears in a menu, a row and a story page. Some words come from the same source. The menu also has its own label.")
("place.workshop", "paragraph", "Open the workshop and try changing each value. Watch which views change and which keep their wording. You can open the code if you want more detail. Your edits stay in that tab and reset when you reload.")
("place.workshop", "fullParagraph", "Start with a story called “What happened”. A web menu calls it “The story”; a row follows the original title. Change one of those values and see what follows—and what keeps its own wording.")
("place.workshop", "fullParagraph", "The living infographic opens the route from meaning to types, projections, contextual overlays, algebra and HTML. An edit returns to its declared source, then the checked process rebuilds and verifies the visible result.")
("place.workshop", "fullParagraph", "This is a small working example of a larger intention: remove unnecessary labour, preserve human authorship, and make the consequences understandable and the evidence inspectable. You can read its rules and source. General programme editing and a complete authoring environment remain future work.")
("place.workshop", "word", "word.source")
("place.workshop", "word", "word.projection")
("place.workshop", "word", "word.overlay")
("place.workshop", "experience", "{\"href\":\"workshop/index.html\",\"label\":\"Open the living infographic\",\"note\":\"Edit two real values. Inspect the source, algebra and generated HTML. Changes stay in your tab; reload to start again.\"}")
("place.workshop", "choice", "place.workshop.choice.0")
("place.workshop.choice.0", "destination", "place.sourcery")
("place.workshop.choice.0", "label", "What should the machine leave to us?")
("place.workshop.choice.0", "kind", "The product philosophy")
("place.workshop", "choice", "place.workshop.choice.1")
("place.workshop.choice.1", "destination", "place.contact")
("place.workshop.choice.1", "label", "What if a polished result misses the point?")
("place.workshop.choice.1", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.workshop", "choice", "place.workshop.choice.2")
("place.workshop.choice.2", "destination", "place.care")
("place.workshop.choice.2", "label", "Who is this helping?")
("place.workshop.choice.2", "kind", "Another way back")
("place.workshop", "choice", "place.workshop.choice.3")
("place.workshop.choice.3", "destination", "place.commons")
("place.workshop.choice.3", "label", "Leave something another person can continue")
("place.workshop.choice.3", "kind", "A path into the wider world")
("place.possibility", "isa", "Place")
("place.possibility", "slug", "possibility")
("place.possibility", "route", "places/possibility.html")
("place.possibility", "title", "What can exist together?")
("place.possibility", "lead", "Some choices work together. Other combinations break a stated rule.")
("place.possibility", "region", "The garden")
("place.possibility", "chapter", "20")
("place.possibility", "source", "note.possibilities")
("place.possibility", "light", "unseen")
("place.possibility", "paragraph", "Start with a simple rule: the two numbers must add up to no more than four. Move the slider to change the limit. The lit pairs show which combinations meet it.")
("place.possibility", "paragraph", "The second view shows a small example from the mathematics of positive responses. Its formula is available if you want it. Neither view tells us which possible state will happen, or whether a real device can reach it.")
("place.possibility", "fullParagraph", "Begin with a small garden of states. Each state carries two quantities. Initially, the declared toy rule permits a total no greater than four. Change the rule and watch the available set change. Then try the positive-response view: the joint relation must also fit the two quantities that support it.")
("place.possibility", "fullParagraph", "The corpus starts its deeper explanation with admission and composition: which states, observables and responses can coexist positively on a declared carrier? Only after those conditions are specified does it ask how the admitted possibilities transform.")
("place.possibility", "fullParagraph", "Notice what the garden has not decided. A permitted state is not necessarily reachable from here, stable over time, preferred by anyone, or realized in the world. Keeping those questions apart makes room for a more exact next step.")
("place.possibility", "word", "word.admissibility")
("place.possibility", "word", "word.positive response")
("place.possibility", "pause", "What can exist together?")
("place.possibility", "instruction", "Move the slider to change the rule. Lit pairs meet the current rule. You can also try a second mathematical view.")
("place.possibility", "supplement", "note.frontier")
("place.possibility", "choice", "place.possibility.choice.0")
("place.possibility.choice.0", "destination", "place.reachable")
("place.possibility.choice.0", "label", "A path is another requirement")
("place.possibility.choice.0", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.possibility", "choice", "place.possibility.choice.1")
("place.possibility.choice.1", "destination", "place.permission")
("place.possibility.choice.1", "label", "Who may choose?")
("place.possibility.choice.1", "kind", "Ideas to compare")
("place.possibility", "choice", "place.possibility.choice.2")
("place.possibility.choice.2", "destination", "place.tiling")
("place.possibility.choice.2", "label", "Let a pattern grow")
("place.possibility.choice.2", "kind", "Follow the research")
("place.reachable", "isa", "Place")
("place.reachable", "slug", "reachable")
("place.reachable", "route", "places/reachable.html")
("place.reachable", "title", "Possible. Permitted. Still out of reach.")
("place.reachable", "lead", "A place can be allowed and still have no available route from here.")
("place.reachable", "region", "The far gate")
("place.reachable", "chapter", "21")
("place.reachable", "source", "note.possibilities")
("place.reachable", "light", "unseen")
("place.reachable", "paragraph", "All three points in the drawing are allowed. At first, the available steps connect A to B, but not B to C. Add the missing step and C becomes reachable from A.")
("place.reachable", "paragraph", "The wider research makes this distinction carefully: being allowed, staying within the rules over time, and being reachable are different requirements. Drawing a desirable destination does not build the bridge.")
("place.reachable", "fullParagraph", "In the investigation framework, possibility, admissibility, viability and reachability are different regions. A state may satisfy the static constraints while no available sequence of controls can reach it from your starting point.")
("place.reachable", "fullParagraph", "A viable history must also remain within its conditions for the required duration. A beautiful endpoint drawn beyond a broken bridge does not supply the missing construction. Declaring a desired optimum cannot replace that bridge.")
("place.reachable", "fullParagraph", "The distinction travels usefully into making things. Name the start, the available actions, the constraints along the way and the evidence of arrival. That is an editorial use of the framework, not a proof that physical and human choices share one dynamics.")
("place.reachable", "word", "word.admissibility")
("place.reachable", "pause", "What can exist together?")
("place.reachable", "instruction", "Add the missing step. See which point you can reach from A.")
("place.reachable", "choice", "place.reachable.choice.0")
("place.reachable.choice.0", "destination", "place.possibility")
("place.reachable.choice.0", "label", "Look back at the allowed space")
("place.reachable.choice.0", "kind", "Another way back")
("place.reachable", "choice", "place.reachable.choice.1")
